            <ArticleTitle>Metastatic pain in the parturient: treatment with patient-controlled epidural sufentanil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>594-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 30-year-old primigravid woman presented at 28 weeks gestation with severe pain related to metastatic gastric carcinoma. Pain control was achieved with epidural sufentanil, administered via a patient-controlled analgesia pump, for 5 days, prior to caesarean delivery. Considerations in deciding the optimal therapeutic regime are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
